.TH AMULEAPI 1 @MAN_DATE@ "aMule REST API daemon v@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "aMule REST API daemon"
.als B_untranslated B
.als RB_untranslated RB
.SH NAME
amuleapi \- the aMule REST API + Server\-Sent Events daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B_untranslated amuleapi
.RB [ \-h " " \fI<host> ]
.RB [ \-p " " \fI<port> ]
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-bind " " \fI<address> ]
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-http\-port " " \fI<num> ]
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-config\-dir " " \fI<path> ]
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-log\-file " " \fI<path> ]
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-no\-log\-file ]
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-foreground ]

.B_untranslated amuleapi
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-set\-admin\-pass " " \fI<plain> ]

.B_untranslated amuleapi
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-set\-guest\-pass " " \fI<plain> ]

.B_untranslated amuleapi
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-version ]

.B_untranslated amuleapi
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-help ]

.B_untranslated amuleapi
.RB_untranslated [ \-\-set\-admin\-pass\-stdin | \-\-set\-guest\-pass\-stdin | \-\-set\-ec\-pass\-stdin ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B_untranslated amuleapi
serves a JSON REST API and a live event stream for a running
\fBamuled\fR(1), so other programs can control aMule over HTTP. It
connects to amuled the same way \fBamulecmd\fR(1) does, and listens on its
own port, so it can run at the same time as \fBamuleweb\fR(1).
.PP
The wire contract for the REST API is documented at
\fIdocs/api/REFERENCE.md\fR; the SSE event catalog lives at
\fIdocs/api/EVENTS.md\fR. See \fIdocs/QUICKSTART\-AMULEAPI.md\fR
for first\-run setup notes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB[ \-h\fR \fI<host>\fR, \fB\-\-host\fR=\fI<host>\fR \fB]\fR
EC host to connect to (default: 127.0.0.1).
.TP
\fB[ \-p\fR \fI<port>\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR=\fI<port>\fR \fB]\fR
EC port on the amuled instance (default: 4712).
.TP
\fB[ \-\-bind\fR=\fI<address>\fR \fB]\fR
HTTP bind address (default: 127.0.0.1, overrides amuleapi.conf
[Server]/BindAddress).
.TP
\fB[ \-\-http\-port\fR=\fI<num>\fR \fB]\fR
HTTP listen port (default: 4713, overrides amuleapi.conf
[Server]/Port).
.TP
\fB[ \-\-config\-dir\fR=\fI<path>\fR \fB]\fR
Path to the amuleapi config dir. Defaults to the same per\-platform
aMule data directory that \fBamuled\fR uses (~/.aMule/ on Linux,
~/Library/Application Support/aMule/ on macOS, %APPDATA%\\aMule\\ on
Windows). Creates the dir with mode 0700 if absent.
.TP
.B_untranslated [ \-\-force\-zlib ]\fR
Always compress the link to \fBamuled\fR(1). By default amuleapi skips
compression when amuled's address is on the local network. Use this when
that address is a VPN tunnel over a slow Internet link.
.TP
.B_untranslated [ \-\-set\-admin\-pass\-stdin ]
Set the admin password from stdin, then exit. Terminal input is hidden and
confirmed; redirected stdin supplies one UTF-8 line without confirmation.
An empty admin password is rejected. EOF and input errors leave credentials
unchanged. No HTTP server or EC connection is started.
.TP
.B_untranslated [ \-\-set\-guest\-pass\-stdin ]
As above for the guest password. An explicitly empty line disables guest access;
EOF does not. Choose exactly one password setter per invocation.
.TP
.B_untranslated [ \-\-set\-ec\-pass\-stdin ]
Read the existing EC password from stdin (hidden on a terminal, without
confirmation), write its MD5 digest to [EC]/PasswordMD5 in amuleapi.conf,
remove the plaintext [EC]/Password key, and exit. Other settings are preserved;
INI formatting and comments may change. Empty input is rejected.
.TP
\fB[ \-\-set\-admin\-pass\fR=\fI<plain>\fR \fB]\fR
Set the admin password to \fI<plain>\fR, storing it salted and
stretched in \fIamuleapi\-passwords\fR (mode 0600), then exit. Does
not start the HTTP server or connect to amuled. A stored password
cannot be read back, only replaced. Prefer the stdin form: literal passwords
can be exposed through process arguments and shell history.
.TP
\fB[ \-\-set\-guest\-pass\fR=\fI<plain>\fR \fB]\fR
Set the guest password to \fI<plain>\fR, storing it the same way, then
exit. An empty \fI<plain>\fR clears the guest password, which is how
guest access is turned off.
.TP
\fB[ \-\-foreground ]\fR
Stay in the foreground (default). aMule does not ship init\-system
units; if you need a system service wrapper, write a downstream unit
that wraps the foreground command.
.TP
\fB[ \-\-log\-file\fR=\fI<path>\fR \fB]\fR
Write a copy of the console output to \fI<path>\fR. On by default at
\fI<config\-dir>/amuleapi.log\fR, so there is always a log to attach to a
bug report; use this to put it somewhere else. It is capped at 10 MiB and
rotated to \fI<path>.1\fR, so it cannot grow without bound. Each line
starts with the local date and time, on the console as well as in the file.
.TP
\fB[ \-\-no\-log\-file ]\fR
Disable the log file entirely and print to the console only, still
timestamped.
.TP
\fB[ \-\-version ]\fR
Print version information and exit.
.TP
\fB[ \-\-help ]\fR
Print a short usage description.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.aMule/amuleapi.conf\fR
Settings file: HTTP address and port, the connection to amuled, login
rate limits and event\-stream sizing. The QUICKSTART document shipped with
the source has the full reference.
.IP
For standalone use, set the EC password with \fB\-\-set\-ec\-pass\-stdin\fR,
or copy its MD5 digest from [EC]/Password in remote.conf to [EC]/PasswordMD5
here. Plaintext [EC]/Password is also supported. Set only one: amuleapi refuses
to start if both are nonempty or PasswordMD5 is not 32 hexadecimal characters.
The digest logs in to amuled just like the password, so keep this file private.
.TP
\fI~/.aMule/amuleapi\-jwt\-secret\fR
Key used to sign login tokens. Created on first launch. Deleting it signs
out everyone.
.TP
\fI~/.aMule/amuleapi\-passwords\fR
The admin and guest passwords, stored so they cannot be read back, only
replaced. This is the only place they are kept. Set them with
\fB\-\-set\-admin\-pass\-stdin\fR / \fB\-\-set\-guest\-pass\-stdin\fR, from the REST API, or
from the Remote Controls preferences in \fBamule\fR(1). A change applies at
the next login and signs out anyone already logged in.
.TP
\fI~/.aMule/amuleapi\-ec\-token\fR
Short\-lived login token, written by \fBamule\fR(1) / \fBamuled\fR(1) when
they start amuleapi themselves. Created fresh each time, read once and
deleted straight away, so an auto\-started amuleapi needs no EC password of
its own. Started by hand, amuleapi finds no token and uses
\fB[EC]/PasswordMD5\fR (or plaintext \fB[EC]/Password\fR) from \fIamuleapi.conf\fR instead. There is no
\fB\-\-password\fR option: a password given on the command line is visible
through \fBps\fR(1) for the lifetime of the process, and can persist
in shell history, service unit files and wrapper scripts.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Please report bugs either on our forum
(\fIhttps://github.com/amule-org/amule/discussions\fR), or in our
bugtracker (\fIhttps://github.com/amule-org/amule/issues\fR).
